{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_igfopik6lkr3mcdgguuukxpt7idzun3ssigxuhd24gmkj32gqkrq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification complete. All four phases pass.\n\n## Result\n\n**No divergences found — the Rust translation matches the C byte-for-byte.** `src/lib.rs` required zero fixes; the one real defect found was in my own harness (see below).\n\n### Artifacts (`translation/`)\n- **`SYMBOLS.md`** — 6 C exports (`create_state`, `destroy_state`, `process_buffer`, `update_flags`, `confuse_types`, `confusion`), all present in the Rust `.so`. Symbol diff **empty**; Rust's only undefined symbols are libc/libgcc/std runtime. Includes the `ProcessState`/bit-field/union layout parity table.\n- **`ERRORS.md`** — 28 rejection rows → 26 tests, all passing.\n- **`CONFIGS.md`** — 27 configuration rows → 26 tests, all passing.\n- **`run_tests.sh`** — builds C + Rust, enumerates feature combos, runs the suite per combo × profile.\n\n### Tests (all via `libloading` on both `.so`s, return value **and** `dup2`-captured stdout compared byte-for-byte)\n59 tests, green across **6 configurations** (`default` / `--no-default-features` / `--all-features` × `release` / `debug`). Cargo.toml declares no `[features]`, so those three are the complete combo set. No driver binary exists in either project (asserted mechanically, so the gate starts failing if one is added).\n\nHeaviest coverage went to the value-dependent UB paths: 2048-point float exponent/mantissa/sign sweep confirming Rust's `f32_to_c_int` reproduces x86-64 `cvttss2si`'s `INT_MIN` \"integer indefinite\" (Rust's saturating `as` would be wrong), all 256 `memchr` target bytes including negative `char` promotion, all 32 bit-field counter start values, out-of-range `switch` selectors, and cross-library `destroy_state`.\n\n### One real problem found (in the harness, not the translation)\n`cargo test` **does not build a `cdylib`** artifact, so the suite was silently loading a stale `target/release/libconfusion_lib.so`. I proved this by injecting three defects into `src/lib.rs` — the suite stayed fully green. Fixed by having `find_rust_so()` refuse to run when the `.so` is older than `src/lib.rs`, plus `run_tests.sh` rebuilding before each run. Re-injecting the same three defects now fails loudly:\n\n| injected defect | caught by |\n|---|---|\n| `mode` bit-field offset 8→9 | 23 Phase-B + 11 Phase-C tests |\n| `f32_to_c_int` → saturating `as c_int` | `row19_row20_confuse_types_float_cast_undefined_range` |\n| `\"Null pointer\"` → `\"null pointer\"` | `row08`/`row09_process_buffer_null_*` |\n\n`tests/phase_0_selfcheck.rs` now locks in these anti-vacuity properties permanently (capture is non-empty and matches expected literal bytes; capture distinguishes different inputs; the two `.so`s are distinct objects).\n\n`c_src/` was not modified."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":950,"cache_read_input_tokens":122974,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":950,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fc5636dc-2417-40c3-a6a3-a3a2b8ac8d43","uuid":"37763c34-7f9b-4e30-91ac-7cdc684240e3","timestamp":"2026-09-05T14:00:15.223Z"}
